# Mojo-first architecture

```text
MOJO = linguagem principal do sistema
PYTHON = escape hatch / interoperabilidade
```

```text
Aplicação Mojo → Interop/Bridge → Python → bibliotecas Python
```

Never invert this. Do not turn the project into Python that calls Mojo.

## Layers

| Layer | Path | Owns | Must not do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Domain | `src/domain/` | types, rules, ports/traits | I/O, Python, vendors |
| Application | `src/application/` | use cases, graph, agents, RAG flow | HTTP/JSON/gRPC, `Python.import_module` |
| Bootstrap | `src/bootstrap/` | composition root | business rules |
| Transport | `src/transport/` | HTTP/gRPC adapters, router, handlers | domain rules |
| Infrastructure | `src/infrastructure/` | Mojo-native I/O, local adapters, IPC, compute | `PythonObject` |
| Interop | `src/interop/python/` | bridges/adapters Mojo → Python | business rules |
| Python | `src/python/` | thin wrappers around Python-only libs | orchestration / domain |

`src/ai_orchestrator/` is legacy Strangler Fig. New Python belongs in `src/python/`.

Python adapters live under `src/python/{agentic,models,training,integrations}` and are reached only through `src/interop/python/*_bridge.mojo`. Do not import Python from `domain/`, `application/`, `bootstrap/`, `transport/`, or `ai_orchestrator/`.

Do **not** put in `src/python/`: HTTP/gRPC servers, Langfuse SDK (use OTEL from Mojo), vLLM (external inference), LiteLLM (external proxy).

## Placement rule

When adding a feature, state the layer and why. Prefer Mojo whenever the work can be done reasonably without a Python-only library (HF, Transformers, ML SDKs, external integrations).

## Boundaries

- Domain and application depend on Mojo abstractions (`Tokenizer`, `LLMProvider`, `VectorStore`), never on `PythonObject`.
- `Python.import_module`, `PythonObject`, and CPython details live only in `src/interop/python/`.
- Bridges hide Python so a later native Mojo implementation can replace the bridge without rewriting callers.

```mojo
var tokenizer = Tokenizer()
var tokens = tokenizer.encode("Hello Mojo")
```
